ap='audits/blind-answers-W04-L18-v1-contracts-reviewer.json';assert sha(ap)=='581ec183121f24e189a963ea5c6c270f9133fd8ad2f4ff1436532e8bb107ccbe'
e=read(ap);answers={a['questionId']:a for a in e['independentAnswers']};obs={o['physicalPage']:o for o in e['sourceObservations']}
assert len(answers)==83 and len(obs)==34
for o in obs.values():assert sha(o['previewPath'])==o['previewSha256']
b=read('audits/review-snapshots/W04-L18-v1-contracts.json');reveal=read('audits/W04-L18-contracts-author-reveal.json');assert sha(reveal['snapshotPath'])==reveal['batchSha256']
manifest=read('audits/W04-L18-frozen-manifest.json');hashes={q['questionId']:q['questionSha256'] for q in manifest['questions']};assert sha('audits/blind-W04-L18.json')==e['blindPacketSha256']==manifest['blindPacketSha256']
flags={}
def flag(n,k,msg):flags.setdefault(f'W04-L18-Q{n:03}',[]).append((k,msg))
flag(5,'distractors','The universal zero-mobility alternative is at least a recognizable misconception, but automatic doubling of every joint freedom and mobility determined only by actuator power are not credible competitors. Replace them with realistic counting errors such as using actuator count alone or summing freedoms without subtracting independent loop constraints. Keep the correct constraint-based key.')
flag(8,'difficulty','This directly distinguishes excess from insufficient task freedom using the definition of redundancy. Mark easy, or require a concrete task-dimension/rank analysis to justify medium.')
flag(11,'difficulty','The multi-select item simply identifies the two complete lists of stated payload factors against two obviously incomplete single-factor claims. Mark easy, or supply a configuration/dynamic counterexample requiring actual comparison if retaining medium.')
flag(18,'difficulty','This is recognition of the slide list of special geometric simplifications, not an application of those geometries. Mark easy, or require reasoning about a concrete transform or axis arrangement to retain medium.')
flag(33,'distractors','Under the explicit equal-link premise, L1+L2 and twice either link length are the same mathematical value. Options o2 and o3 therefore duplicate one another. Replace one with a distinct plausible mistaken inner radius and update its rationale.')
flag(51,'distractors','Electrical motor failure, undefined forward position and physically removing a joint are not strong competing interpretations of Jacobian rank loss. Use credible alternatives such as joint-coordinate dimension loss, loss of all task directions, or global unreachability of every nearby position, carefully keeping them false under the stated local task.')
flag(51,'difficulty','The current question asks only the definition of singular task-rank loss. Mark easy, or use a specific matrix/task direction to create a genuine medium application.')
flag(55,'distractors','A negative determinant for a nonsquare matrix and an exact physical joint count are implausible rivals to Gram-matrix row dependence. Replace them with realistic rank/nullspace confusions, for example column dependence in a redundant full-row-rank matrix, or exactly one lost direction when the rank deficit is unspecified. Keep the all-zero claim only as one distinct stronger-than-necessary misconception.')
flag(57,'difficulty','The required condition for an ordinary matrix inverse is direct prerequisite recognition. Mark easy, or introduce competing task dimensions or a concrete configuration-dependent Jacobian to justify medium.')
flag(64,'distractors','Two alternatives, r²=9+sin(theta2) and r²=81cos(theta1), can be dismissed without performing the intended expansion. Use credible expansion mistakes, such as omitting the factor 2 in the cross term or reversing its sign, while retaining the absolute-versus-relative-angle alternative.')
flag(66,'explanation','The working says the radii are sqrt(0.72), 1, 9 and 5 respectively, but the frozen option order is (1,0), (0,9), (3,4), (0.6,0.6). Correct the mapping to 1, 9, 5, sqrt(0.72), or explicitly name each target. Prefer named coordinates so option shuffling cannot invalidate the explanation. The key and individual option rationales are otherwise correct.')
flag(70,'difficulty','The literal unescaped newline inside a short quoted string is a direct syntax-recognition task. Mark easy, or require comparing valid continuation/escape forms for a medium item.')
flag(71,'difficulty','Counting two explicitly stated 200-element nested loops is a single product, 200 times 200. Mark easy, or add an actual indentation/filter/storage mutation requiring more tracing to retain medium.')
flag(76,'distractors','The correct sampled-boundary result is good, but sampling expands the workspace and the grid stops at pi/2 are not credible alternatives to the displayed full interval. Replace these with realistic endpoint-count or half-step mistakes, such as using 200 instead of 199 or one full grid step instead of the nearest half-step, with accurate numerical reasoning.')
flag(77,'difficulty','This is direct scaling of the same Cartesian-product count already established by Q071: doubling both dimensions multiplies by four. Mark easy, or add a meaningful independent complexity/storage variation to retain medium.')
flag(82,'distractors','The spherical workspace creates three extra freedoms and one radial slide controls roll/pitch/yaw alternatives are implausible. Use believable tool/task-symmetry misconceptions, such as confusing free axial roll with free tool-axis direction or assuming positional reachability guarantees the prescribed axis direction. Preserve the distinction between the pictured three-motion positioner and an added orienting wrist.')
flag(83,'difficulty','The stem supplies det J=l1*l2*sin(theta2), so answering requires only identifying the zeros of sine, not a hard Jacobian derivation. Prefer a genuine derivation task that omits this result and compares full Jacobian/determinant combinations; alternatively relabel and remove the instruction to differentiate.')
flag(83,'explanation','For a task advertised as differentiating the forward map, the solution must display the actual four Jacobian entries and enough determinant expansion to verify the cancellation. It currently only instructs the learner to differentiate and reports the final determinant. Add the full fixed-frame matrix with definitions/units and then show the straight/folded rank-loss conclusion.')
reviews=[]
for q in b['questions']:
 a=answers[q['id']];assert question_hash(q)==hashes[q['id']]==a['questionSha256'];assert set(q['correctOptionIds'])==set(a['answerOptionIds']);assert R not in {q['authorId'],*q.get('revisionAuthors',[])}
 checks={k:True for k in ['sourceSupport','assumptions','answerSet','distractors','calculations','figureFidelity','explanation','difficulty','duplication']}
 for k,_ in flags.get(q['id'],[]):checks[k]=False
 pages=sorted({c['physicalPage'] for c in q['citations']})
 reason=a['reasoning']+' All cited actual source pixels were inspected before the independent-answer freeze. No L18 author key, solution, generator, author checks or author findings were opened before all 83 answers and the reviewer-owned calculations were saved. Printed course statements and worked examples were visible, so blindness concerns the question author key rather than the source itself. After reveal, all option rationales, relevant formula variables/units/conditions, source qualifiers, difficulty and duplication were checked. Reviewer checks passed 42 symbolic/code assertions and 1,000 random radial identities, and an independently produced workspace plot was visually compared with the actual source plot. Non-numerical recall items do not require numerical calculation; non-figure items have no additional figure-fidelity requirement. Questions that apply a concept to a diagram, numeric case, task qualification or code mutation are distinct only when a real new reasoning operation is required. '+('The listed defects prevent approval despite agreement with the intended key.' if q['id'] in flags else 'All nine criteria pass for this exact object; this does not certify complete lecture or full-course coverage.')
 reviews.append(dict(id=q['id']+'-v1-contracts-independent',questionId=q['id'],questionVersion=q['version'],questionSha256=question_hash(q),reviewerId=R,decision='flagged' if q['id'] in flags else 'verified',reviewedAt=now,sourceVersions=e['sourceVersions'],reviewedSlideIds=[f'lectures-p{p:04}' for p in pages],independentAnswerOptionIds=a['answerOptionIds'],solvedBeforeAnswerSeen=True,checks=checks,reasoning=reason,findings=[msg for _,msg in flags.get(q['id'],[])],blindAnswersPath=ap,blindAnswersSha256=sha(ap),independentSolvedAt=e['answersFrozenAt'],priorAuthorExposure=False,sourceAnswerExposure='Printed source statements and worked examples were visible during source-first solving; no question-author keys or solutions were exposed.',computationsPath='audits/W04-L18-independent-checks.json',sourceInspectionEvidence=[dict(inspectorId=R,**{k:obs[p][k] for k in ['physicalPage','previewPath','previewSha256','dimensions','inspectedAt']}) for p in pages]))
errors=[x for rv in reviews for x in schema_errors(rv,read('data/schema.review.json'))];assert not errors,errors
out='data/reviews/W04-L18-v1-independent-contracts.json';write(out,reviews)
rb={r['questionId']:r for r in reviews};qs=copy.deepcopy(b['questions']);cs=copy.deepcopy(b['concepts'])
for q in qs:q['status']=rb[q['id']]['decision'];q['reviewIds']=[rb[q['id']]['id']]
verified={q['id'] for q in qs if q['status']=='verified'}
for c in cs:c['status']='verified' if any(qid in verified for qid in c['questionIds']) else 'drafted'
sm=read('sources/manifest.json');slides=[json.loads(line) for sid in ['lectures','assignments'] for line in (ROOT/f'sources/page_maps/{sid}.jsonl').read_text().splitlines()]
updates={s['id']:s for s in read('data/inspection-batches/W04-L18.json')['slides']};slides=[copy.deepcopy(updates.get(s['id'],s)) for s in slides]
for slide in slides:
 if slide['id'] in updates:slide['conceptIds']=[c['id'] for c in cs if slide['id'] in c['slideIds']]
tmp={'schemaVersion':'1.0.0','bankVersion':'L18-v1-contracts-independent-isolated','title':'L18 independent review validation','complete':False,'sources':sm['sources'],'assets':sm['assets'],'slides':slides,'questions':qs,'concepts':cs,'reviews':reviews,'learningTools':{k:[] for k in ['formulaSheet','confusionPairs','traps','algorithmVisualizations','numericalFamilies']}}
v=validate_bank(tmp,ROOT,check_files=True)
coverage=[{'id':'L18-COVERAGE-01','status':'open','sourcePages':[548],'finding':'The explicit iterative design process and its joint-number/arrangement/actuation/sensing decisions appear in a concept description and solution but are not independently tested: Q003 only contrasts task domains. Add a meaningful design-refinement scenario that distinguishes revisiting coupled mechanical/actuation/sensing choices from treating a first choice as final.'},{'id':'L18-COVERAGE-02','status':'open','sourcePages':[558,560],'finding':'The source-specific articulated aliases (jointed, elbow, anthropomorphic) and the SCARA expansion are present in sources or explanations but not tested by an answer choice. A single well-designed terminology/matching question can close these explicit nomenclature facts without creating several near-duplicate recall items.'},{'id':'L18-COVERAGE-03','status':'repair_linked','sourcePages':[568,570],'finding':'Q083 currently exposes the Jacobian determinant before answering and does not show the full matrix in its solution. Strengthen that flagged item into the genuine fixed-frame differentiation/determinant angle, rather than adding another roots-of-sine paraphrase.'},{'id':'L18-COVERAGE-04','status':'bounded_accounting_note','sourcePages':list(range(544,578)),'finding':'All 34 actual pages were personally inspected. Pages544–546 are title/outcome/outline,576 reference and577 closing. Pages547–574 contain substantive content and575 is a recap; all29 substantive/recap pages have at least one draft citation. The46 concept records are clusters rather than proof that every atomic fact is fully assessed. The source qualifications are preserved, including numbering conflicts, task-relative redundancy, guaranteed versus local payload, signed-DH conventions, wrist scope, task normalization, inertia interpretation and finite versus continuous sampling.'}]
summary=dict(reviewerId=R,completedAt=now,questionsReviewed=83,verified=len(verified),flagged=len(flags),keyDisagreements=0,actualPagesInspected=34,reviewFile=out,reviewSha256=sha(out),blindAnswersSha256=sha(ap),independentChecks='audits/W04-L18-independent-checks.json',flaggedQuestionIds=list(flags),findings=[{'questionId':id,'criteria':[k for k,_ in fs],'findings':[msg for _,msg in fs]} for id,fs in flags.items()],coverageChallenge=coverage,validation=v,sourceQualifications='Preserve all12 author sourceIssues and the independent page observations; none were silently globally resolved.',mutations='Only reviewer audit, check-script, review and handoff files; no question, canonical bank, source or Git edits.')
write('audits/W04-L18-contracts-review-summary.json',summary)
(ROOT/'docs/handoffs/L18-contracts-review.md').write_text(f'# L18 independent review frozen\n\n{len(verified)} verified and {len(flags)} flagged out of 83, with no key disagreements. All 34 actual pages 544–577 were inspected. Reviewer-owned checks passed 42 symbolic/code assertions and 1,000 random radial identities. The maximum sampled radius is 8.999723083556866, not the continuous maximum 9.\n\nReview: data/reviews/W04-L18-v1-independent-contracts.json. Exact findings and coverage challenge: audits/W04-L18-contracts-review-summary.json. Answer freeze: audits/blind-answers-W04-L18-v1-contracts-reviewer.json. The keyed snapshot and reveal record preserve provenance.\n\nDefinite repairs include duplicate equal-link distractors in Q033, an incorrectly ordered respectively list in Q066, and the pre-exposed determinant/incomplete full-matrix derivation in Q083. Other findings address weak alternatives and inflated difficulty. Preserve the {len(verified)} accepted correctness hashes. Two small coverage gaps remain: iterative design decisions and a combined source-specific terminology match. Strengthen Q083 to close the full-Jacobian angle rather than adding a duplicate.\n\nNo author content, bank, source or Git changes. Next priority is the first independent L19 review from its answer-free frozen packet, before opening any keyed L19 material.\n')
